      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why does start with __ and the other one with _. Is there some naming scheme documented anywhere that would prevent collisions between local a global headers? I see both __ and _ used in existing headers under /include, but I also see _LINUX used as a prefix on headers in /drivers and not on headers in /include/linux.",
