      "writtenOn": "2020-09-22T22:31:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I went for the existing convention used in the Trusty code: the headers in include/linux/trusty/ use \"__LINUX_TRUSTY\", and the headers in drivers/trusty/ use \"_TRUSTY\".\n\nUnfortunately there\u0027s no include guard naming convention that all Linux kernel code uses.  So it\u0027s not worth overthinking this.  Using the directory name in the name for include/ (shared headers) but not for other directories (private headers) seems fairly common, though.",
      "parentUuid": "800ac8c6_e9dbbf13",
